# Cypress Test Automation Project

This project contains automated **Frontend and API tests** using **Cypress**, **Cucumber**, and **Allure Report**.

The project follows a structured approach for automated testing, separating API services, step definitions, feature files, and test scenarios.

# Prerequisites

Before running the project, make sure you have the following installed:

- Node.js
- npm
- Git

You can verify your installations by running:

```bash
node --version
npm --version
git --version
```

---

# Clone the Repository

Clone the repository using:

```bash
git clone <REPOSITORY_URL>
```

Then navigate to the project directory:

```bash
cd project-folder-name
```

Example:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/your-repository.git
cd your-repository
```

---

# Install Dependencies

After cloning the repository and accessing the project folder, install all project dependencies:

```bash
npm install
```

This command installs all dependencies defined in the project's `package.json`.

If Cypress needs to be installed manually:

```bash
npm install cypress --save-dev
```

---

# Run Cypress

## Open Cypress in Interactive Mode

```bash
npx cypress open
```

---

# Run the Complete Test Suite

To execute all tests:

```bash
npx cypress run
```

If the project contains a test script configured in `package.json`:

```bash
npm test
```

---

# Run a Specific Feature

To execute a specific feature file:

```bash
npx cypress run --spec "cypress/e2e/path/to/feature.feature"
```

Example:

```bash
npx cypress run --spec "cypress/e2e/api/cart/createCart.feature"
```

Another example:

```bash
npx cypress run --spec "cypress/e2e/api/cart/cancelPurchase.feature"
```

---

# Allure Report

Allure Report is used to generate detailed and interactive test execution reports.

## Install Allure

```bash
npm install --save-dev allure-commandline
```

## Generate the Allure Report

After executing the tests:

```bash
npx allure generate allure-results --clean -o allure-report
```

The report will be generated inside:

```text
allure-report
```

## Open the Allure Report

```bash
npx allure open allure-report
```

## Complete Test Execution and Reporting Flow

Run all tests:

```bash
npx cypress run
```

Generate the report:

```bash
npx allure generate allure-results --clean -o allure-report
```

Open the report:

```bash
npx allure open allure-report
```

---

# Frontend Test Scenario Example

## Scenario: Successfully Login with Valid Credentials

```gherkin
Feature: Login

Scenario: Successfully login with valid credentials

  Given I access the login page
  When I enter a valid email
  And I enter a valid password
  And I click on the login button
  Then I should be logged in successfully
```

## Test Flow

```text
User accesses the application
        ↓
User navigates to the Login page
        ↓
User enters a valid email
        ↓
User enters a valid password
        ↓
User clicks the Login button
        ↓
The system authenticates the user
        ↓
The user is redirected to the authenticated area
```

---

# API Test Scenario Example

## Scenario: Successfully Create a Shopping Cart

```gherkin
Feature: Shopping Cart

Scenario: Successfully create a shopping cart

  Given an authenticated user exists
  And an available product exists
  When I create a shopping cart with the product
  Then the cart should be created successfully
```

## Test Flow

```text
Create a new user
        ↓
Validate HTTP status 201
        ↓
Authenticate the user
        ↓
Receive the authentication token
        ↓
Create an available product
        ↓
Validate HTTP status 201
        ↓
Retrieve the product ID
        ↓
Create a shopping cart containing the product
        ↓
Send the authentication token
        ↓
Validate HTTP status 201
        ↓
Validate the cart ID and success message
```

---

# Purchase Cancellation and Stock Restoration Example

## Scenario: Restore Product Stock When Cancelling a Purchase

```gherkin
Scenario: Should restore product stock when cancelling a purchase

  Given an authenticated user with an existing cart
  When I complete the purchase
  And I cancel the purchase
  Then the product stock should be restored
```

## Test Flow

```text
Create a new user
        ↓
Authenticate the user
        ↓
Retrieve the authentication token
        ↓
Create a product with available stock
        ↓
Create a shopping cart
        ↓
Complete the purchase
        ↓
The product stock is updated
        ↓
Cancel the purchase
        ↓
The product stock is restored
        ↓
Validate the original product quantity
```

